I just researched this last night.

Carry capacity in nh3.1.0 is
	50 + 50*(STR + CON)/2
to a maximum of 1000.

STR in this formula is a "flattened" strength:
	18/01 to 18/31 => 19
	18/32 to 18/81 => 20
	18/82 to 18/100 => 21

You're burdened when you're carrying from 1.0 to 1.5 times your carry
capacity; stressed is 1.5 to 2.0; etc.

Note that you get max carry with 18/32 STR and 18 CON:
	50 + 50*(20 + 18)/2 = 1000
or with 18/82 STR and 17 CON:
	50 + 50*(21 + 17)/2 = 1000
